   "title": "Note: About",
   "color": "#222",
   "bgcolor": "#000",
   "properties": {
    "Node name for S&R": "MarkdownNote"
   },
   "widgets_values": [
    "## Depth Anything 3 (mono) → Mesh\n\nSingle image → metric-consistent geometry → mesh (GLB) + preview render.\n\n**How it works**\n1. `Load DA3 Model` picks the Depth-Anything-3 checkpoint (`depth_anything_3_mono_large`).\n2. `DA3 Inference` runs in **mono** mode at 504 px on the longest side.\n3. `DA3 Geometry To Mesh` back-projects the depth + confidence into a triangle mesh\n   (`decimation 1`, `discontinuity 0.04`, `confidence 0.1`, sky mask on, texture on).\n4. `Render Mesh` and `DA3 Render (depth_colored)` show the result; `Save GLB` exports it.\n\n**Defaults**: resolution 504, decimation 1, discontinuity 0.04, confidence 0.10, sky mask on.\nRaise `resolution` to 756–1008 for finer relief (slower), raise `decimation` to 2–4 for a lighter GLB.\n\n**Note**: a single view only reconstructs the visible shell — the back side is open, which is expected\nfor monocular depth. Use a subject that fills the frame with a clean silhouette."
   ]
  },
